cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use geoCensor, please cite it as below."
title: "geoCensor: Censoring-Aware Analysis of USGS National Geochemical Database Data"
abstract: >-
  An R package for parsing, modelling, and visualising left- and right-censored
  element concentrations from the U.S. Geological Survey National Geochemical
  Database (NGDB) and similar datasets, including detection-limit parsing and
  censoring-aware maximum-likelihood lognormal geometric means by state.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Edwards
    given-names: Ross
    email: pedwards5@wisc.edu
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-30"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/diskoisland/geoCensor"
repository-code: "https://github.com/diskoisland/geoCensor"
keywords:
  - geochemistry
  - censored data
  - maximum likelihood
  - detection limits
  - silver
  - USGS NGDB
